       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg TID. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. Even in the most liberal practice, the ceiling is about 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** this is twice the maximum daily dose. It raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg BID\n- Another dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg TID is what you intend, tell me and include a brief rationale for the order note. I'll then enter it as written."
